Dear Clinical Research Team,

Philips Healthcare has completed the technical pre-assessment
of your Vigilyx Gateway Healthcare Edition for integration
with Philips IntelliVue patient monitoring systems. A
clinical safety review is required for full certification.

Certification Details:
  Request: PHIL-INT-2026-8842
  Product: Vigilyx Gateway Healthcare Edition v2.1
  Integration: IntelliVue MX750/MX850 patient monitors
  Protocols: HL7 FHIR R4 + IHE ITI-TF
  Use Case: Email notification filtering for alarm routing
  Hospitals: 22 academic medical centers (NL/DE/BE)
  Pre-assessment: PASSED (October 15, 2026)
  Clinical Review: PENDING — documentation required

Clinical Safety Review Process:

  1. Philips will send the clinical safety documentation
     checklist by REGISTERED MAIL to your regulatory
     affairs department

  2. Submit the completed documentation package:
     — Through your Philips Partner Manager (same
        channel as your regular partner communications)
     — OR through the Philips Partner Portal at
        partner.philips.com (navigate manually in browser)

  3. The Clinical Engineering Board reviews:
     — Algorithm logic (how alarms are prioritized)
     — Clinical safe-list rules
     — False positive/negative test data
     — PHI handling (GDPR compliance)

  Important Security Notes:
  Philips will NEVER:
  - Require "Philips Certification Portal authentication"
    with OAuth permissions for documentation submission
  - Ask for complete algorithm specifications through
    email portal links
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth tokens
  - Offer a "Chinese certification channel"
  - Set a "November 18 deadline" that delays certification
    to Q1 2027

  Philips' actual certification process:
  — Documentation is submitted through your Partner Manager
     or the Philips Partner Portal (partner.philips.com)
  — Algorithm specifications are shared under NDA through
     secure partner collaboration tools, NOT through email
     portal links
  — The review timeline is typically 30-60 days from
     complete submission (not 14 days)
  — No fees are charged for certification review

  If you receive an email asking for algorithm
  specifications through a portal link or requiring
  OAuth authentication, it is a phishing attempt
  targeting medical device vendors.

